        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "cf75be6f-fe7c-5cc2-8f7c-c102f4c3acc6",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Graham Hill, Richie Ginther, Bruce McLaren\n- Events: 1962 Italian Grand Prix, 1963 Lombank Trophy, 2009 Monaco Grand Prix\n- Roles: racing driver, team owner\n- Places: England, Monaco, Circuit de Monaco\n- Products: BRM P57, Cooper\n\nFacts:\n- Graham Hill was born on 15 February 1929 and was a British racing driver and team owner from England.\n- Graham Hill was twice Formula One World Champion.\n- At the 1962 Italian Grand Prix, Graham Hill's teammate Richie Ginther finished second and Cooper driver Bruce McLaren finished third.\n- The 1963 Lombank Trophy was run over 50 laps and was won by British driver Graham Hill in a BRM P57.\n- The 2009 Monaco Grand Prix was a Formula One motor race held on 24 May 2009 at the Circuit de Monaco in Monaco.\n- Graham Hill died on 29 November 1975.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
